{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I shall see him.</b> I see the praise and greatness of Jacob — but not now; rather, after a time." "<b>From Jacob a star.</b> As its Targum renders — the sense of ״דָּרַךְ קַשְׁתּוֹ״ (Lamentations 2), that the star passes like an arrow; דישט\"נט בְּלַעַ\"ז, that is, a constellation shall arise." "<b>And a scepter shall arise.</b> A king who rules and dominates." "<b>And crush the temples of Moab.</b> This is David, about whom it says ״the הַשְׁכֵּב אוֹתָם אַרְצָה וַיְמַדֵּד שְׁנֵי חֲבָלִים לְהָמִית״ etc. (II Samuel 8)." "<b>And break down.</b> A term of hollowing out / carving, as in ״אֲנִי קַרְתִּי״ (II Kings 19), ״מַקֶּבֶת בּוֹר נֻקַּרְתֶּם״ (Isaiah 51), ״יִקְּרוּהָ עֹרְבֵי נַחַל״ (Proverbs 30); פורי\"ר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>All the sons of Seth.</b> All the nations — for all of them issued from Seth, son of the first man."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French destendre, 'to shoot (a bow)' or possibly destenant, present participle.", 4 "the la'az is Old French forer, 'to bore/pierce'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:50.583000214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}